dmarc-srg v2.3: remove xml_parser_free() call in ReportData::fromXmlFile()

PHP 8.5 deprecated xml_parser_free() (the function has been a no-op since
PHP 8.0). dmarc-srg's init.php error handler turns every E_DEPRECATED into
an ErrorException, so on PHP >= 8.5 the call aborts parsing of every DMARC
report - fatal for fetch_reports.php and for report display in the web UI.

Deleting the line is exactly what upstream did on master (zero
xml_parser_free references remain there); the fix is simply unreleased as
of v2.3, which is still GitHub releases/latest.

Retire this patch when DMARC_SRG_VERSION moves to a release containing the
upstream fix (>= 3.0) - the build fails loudly if it no longer applies.

--- a/classes/Report/ReportData.php
+++ b/classes/Report/ReportData.php
@@ -82,7 +82,6 @@
                 }
             }
         } finally {
-            xml_parser_free($parser);
             unset($parser);
         }
         return $rdata;
